 "fx_note": "Nothing that moves by nature is in the paint; these move it. The river: river-shimmer, glints that come and drift downstream (up the picture and to the right, toward the bend) over the painting's own still sparkle, the barge a hole in it; barge-ripples (two) where the water laps along the barge between it and the quay; steps-ripples at the foot of the landing's steps, in the very corner (clipped to the stair and the water seen past the quay's edge; under the inventory bar while the game waits for a click). The barge rides at its moorings: barge-bob (ENGINE-13R's bob, as the brief gives it), the water painted whole under it, and the curb cut-out in front of the foot of its bow, so that a pixel up or down shows only water and stone. The five hens: one flock of one each (so that each keeps her own colouring and her place in the row, which runs from in front of the coop back toward the house), depth true (sized by their row from frames sizeAt 590), shy 0, never flying, turning or pecking: they stand, look up and shuffle, facing west over the river at the city. The washing sways on its line (washing-sway, its cut-out hung from the top). A thin cooking smoke rises behind the houses beyond the house of prayer (plane back). Swallows over the river and the far bank: the temple steps' swallow frames (rome_steps_birds.py), from that scene's folder.",
